description "Network policy: LLMNR off, and resolv.conf pointed at the systemd-resolved stub"

supports "fedora" "rhel" "debian" "ubuntu"

// The `resolv.conf` link this ships is the same `L+` line `deb/bootc-base`
// already writes at `00-resolv-conf.conf`, for the same reason and to the same
// target. Two tmpfiles rules naming one path is not a collision — different
// filenames, identical content, the second a no-op — and neither module can
// drop it: the base needs it to boot with a resolver at all, and this module
// needs it on Fedora where the base does not ship one. EL ships no
// systemd-resolved, so the link would leave a `rhel` machine with no resolver.
//
// The NetworkManager drop-in is inert where NetworkManager is absent, which on
// a deb image it is until `desktop-environment/kde-plasma` installs it. That is exactly the image
// where LLMNR being on would matter.
